# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.local is now GENERATED by Terraform — you no longer copy this file.
#
# Running `make dev` (or `make reset`) applies infra/terraform/envs/local, which
# provisions the LocalStack S3 buckets AND writes a fresh .env.local from the
# template at infra/terraform/templates/env.local.tftpl. This kills the old
# manual two-file drift between .env.local and api/.env.
#
# To change a dev value: edit infra/terraform/envs/local/env-files.tf (values)
# and/or the template (shape), then re-run `make dev`. The authoritative list of
# variables lives in api/src/lib/env.ts (zod schema) — add a var THERE and in
# the template together.
#
# `make snapshot` still needs prod RDS creds; export them in your shell (not in
# .env.local, which is regenerated): DB_HOST_PROD / DB_NAME_PROD / DB_USER_PROD
# / DB_PASSWORD_PROD. The DB password lives in Secrets Manager — fetch manually.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
